RELATIONAL HORIZON  h[x]
============================================================
  h[x] is the minimal closure-geodesic distance from x to any
  point where the coordinate metric dq becomes undefined or
  divergent.  The level set h[x] = h0 is the relational event
  horizon separating RDG-exterior geometry from the Q-box
  interior.

BASE SETS
---------
  I        = inverse-limit index set from refinement system {G_h}
  Q        = Q-box interior (uninspectable region)
  E        = I \ Q  (RDG exterior)

DISTANCES
---------
  1. Closure geodesic distance:
       dΓ(A,B) = inf_{x(0)=A, x(T)=B} ∫_0^T CΓ(x(t), ẋ(t)) dt

  2. Discounted closure trajectory distance:
       dΓ^(λ)(x,y) = ∫_0^∞ e^{-λ t} || Γ_t(x) - Γ_t(y) || dt   (λ > 0)

  3. Constructed coordinate metric (depth–refinement–constraint):
       dq(x,y) = coordinate-induced metric
                 (may diverge or be undefined near Q)

KEY PRINCIPLE
-------------
  Relational geometry uses dΓ.
  Coordinate geometry uses dq.
  The horizon is where dq fails but dΓ remains finite.

DEFINITION OF RELATIONAL THICKNESS
----------------------------------
  For any x ∈ I:

      h[x] := inf_{y ∈ Q} { dΓ(x,y)  |  dq(x,y) = ∞ }

  Interpretation:
    - Search over all interior points y ∈ Q.
    - Require dq(x,y) = ∞ (coordinate metric breaks).
    - Measure relational distance dΓ(x,y) (still finite).
    - The smallest such dΓ is the horizon thickness at x.

ALTERNATE FORM (DISCOUNTED METRIC)
----------------------------------
  h[x] := inf_{y ∈ Q} { dΓ^(λ)(x,y) | dq(x,y) = ∞ }

  Same meaning:
    finite relational separation,
    infinite coordinate separation.

EVENT HORIZON SET
-----------------
  Choose critical thickness h0 > 0.

      H := { x ∈ I | h[x] = h0 }

  Interpretation:
    - H is the relational event horizon.
    - Inside H: dq fails, Q-box interior.
    - Outside H: dq stable, RDG geometry valid.

GEOMETRIC INTERPRETATION
------------------------
  - dΓ finite  → relationally reachable
  - dq infinite → coordinate geometry breaks
  - h[x] measures how close x is to the breakdown boundary
  - H is the boundary where RDG geometry collapses
  - Q is the interior beyond inspection

